      "end": 55.8,
      "duration": 53.93,
      "text": "Greetings, colleagues. My topic is AI and the youth shaping the next generation. My name is Dr. Tandai Zengany and I'm a lecturer at Africa University in Zimbabwe, as well as a member of the UNESCO Women for Ethical AI. And I'm also a member of UNESCO's Ethical AI experts without borders, as well as an alumni of African Women in Tech and AI, where I was trained at the International Center for Artificial Intelligence in Morocco. My work focuses on AI ethics research among other disciplines like high-speed optical communications, where I did my studies in Malaysia and Greece. I'm here today, not just as an expert, but as an advocate for the immense potential of Zimbabwean youth.",
