      "fragment_index": 3,
      "start": 108.3,
      "end": 166.52,
      "duration": 58.22,
      "text": "The risk of displacement. For a young graduate entering the job market, AI's automation of tasks in sectors like data entry, customer service and even basic coding is a genuine concern. It can feel like the goalposts are moving just as they are about to score. The risk isn't just job loss. It's a potential erosion of creative confidence. If AI can generate art, if it can generate music and essays in seconds, what is the value of human creativity? This can lead to a dependency where we stop exercising our own creative muscles, the very muscles that make us innovative and resilient. However, focusing on the risks is a disservice to our youth. The real conversation is about transition and not replacement.",
