      "end": 413.78,
      "duration": 61.25,
      "text": "How does this reflect our Ubuntu principles? And then next we need to create STEM boxes for innovation. Young people need safe spaces to experiment, to fail, to unlearn. This means supporting local hackathons, incubators and innovation hubs focused on solving African problems like using AI for drug resistant crop analysis, diagnosing local diseases or preserving indigenous languages. Then we need to demand a seat at the table. Finally, we must encourage young innovators to not just build apps but to actively engage in policy discussions. They must be in the room when regulations are drafted to ensure their voices shape the governance of technology that will define their lives. So the goal is to foster a generation of techno optimists with a critical lens.",
